699
00:36:11.113 --> 00:36:11.966
Pros:

700
00:36:12.246 --> 00:36:13.313
Fast, simple.

701
00:36:13.593 --> 00:36:14.403
Cons:

702
00:36:14.683 --> 00:36:16.219
Unbounded business risk.

703
00:36:16.499 --> 00:36:17.310
Verdict:

704
00:36:17.590 --> 00:36:19.489
Rejected: caused the incident.

705
00:36:19.769 --> 00:36:24.142
In-memory snapshot + event refresh + DB fallback for fresh.

706
00:36:24.422 --> 00:36:25.275
Pros:

707
00:36:25.555 --> 00:36:29.331
Fast, bounded staleness, survives DB outage for browse.

708
00:36:29.611 --> 00:36:30.422
Cons:

709
00:36:30.702 --> 00:36:33.305
More moving parts; needs staleness metrics.

710
00:36:33.585 --> 00:36:34.395
Verdict:

711
00:36:34.675 --> 00:36:35.486
Chosen.

712
00:36:36.836 --> 00:36:37.519
8.

713
00:36:37.799 --> 00:36:38.951
Failure modes.

714
00:36:39.231 --> 00:36:43.241
Kafka down, then 30 s full reload still bounds browse staleness.

715
00:36:43.521 --> 00:36:53.079
DB down, then browse serves last snapshot (alert when age 90 s); fresh checks fail closed after the 80 ms timeout (see ADR).

716
00:36:53.359 --> 00:36:57.711
Pod starts with no snapshot, then readiness probe fails until first load.

717
00:36:57.991 --> 00:36:58.695
10.

718
00:36:58.975 --> 00:37:15.295
Observability. serviceability.snapshot.age.seconds (gauge, alert 90 s), serviceability.snapshot.version, serviceability.lookupconsistency,result (counter or timer), serviceability.fresh.db (timer, with outcome tag).

719
00:37:16.645 --> 00:37:17.477
11.

720
00:37:17.757 --> 00:37:18.589
Rollout.

721
00:37:18.869 --> 00:37:27.103
Feature flag serviceability.fresh-check.enabled in checkout; shadow-compare old versus new answers for 1 week; then enforce.

722
00:37:27.383 --> 00:37:28.237
14.

723
00:37:28.517 --> 00:37:31.226
Decision (ADR-011 summary).

724
00:37:31.506 --> 00:37:41.789
Consistency is chosen per use case: browse gets bounded staleness ( at most 60 s) served from memory; checkout gets a fresh read from the source of truth.

725
00:37:42.069 --> 00:37:47.743
When a fresh check can't be answered in time, checkout fails closed (rejects with a retryable error).

726
00:37:48.023 --> 00:37:51.629
An undeliverable paid order costs more than a retried checkout.

