893
00:49:12.934 --> 00:49:14.299
ADR-011:

894
00:49:14.579 --> 00:49:16.713
Serviceability consistency levels.

895
00:49:16.993 --> 00:49:17.910
Context.

896
00:49:18.190 --> 00:49:21.411
Serviceability is read ~10⁶ times per write.

897
00:49:21.691 --> 00:49:28.177
Stale answers at checkout cause paid, undeliverable orders (incident, 1,900 orders).

898
00:49:28.457 --> 00:49:31.806
The DB must not be a hard dependency for browsing.

899
00:49:32.086 --> 00:49:32.961
Decision.

900
00:49:33.241 --> 00:49:45.678
(1) Browse is served from a per-pod in-memory snapshot, refreshed by events (~1 to 2 s) and a 30 s full reload, so staleness is at most 60 s including one missed reload.

901
00:49:45.958 --> 00:49:50.225
(2) Checkout does a fresh primary-key read with an 80 ms budget.

902
00:49:50.505 --> 00:49:56.393
(3) When a fresh check is unavailable, checkout fails closed with a retryable 503.

903
00:49:56.673 --> 00:49:59.723
(4) Rollout is SHADOW for one week, then ENFORCE.

904
00:50:01.073 --> 00:50:02.119
Consequences.

905
00:50:02.399 --> 00:50:05.492
(+) Browse survives DB and Kafka outages.

906
00:50:05.772 --> 00:50:09.399
(+) Checkout correctness no longer depends on cache freshness.

907
00:50:09.679 --> 00:50:27.983
(minus ) Checkout availability now includes serviceability + its DB (99.95 % times 99.95 % about 99.9 % for this step), accepted because a failed checkout is retryable and an undeliverable order is not.

908
00:50:28.263 --> 00:50:32.295
(minus ) One more Kafka topic and an outbox relay to operate.

909
00:50:32.575 --> 00:50:44.351
Revisit when: serviceability moves from pincode to geofence polygons (dataset grows ~1000 times ), or checkout volume grows past what PK reads can serve.

